Q: Event emitter in router-outlet for getting value from child to parent A: <p>If you don't want to use the <code>(activate)</code> event or a shared service you can make use of <code>[routerOutletData]</code>. In the parent component you define the method that you want to be executed:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export class ParentComponent {
    // Function that you want to run when event on child occours
    onEvent = (data: DataType) =&gt; {
        // Whatever you want to do with the data
        ...
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>In the template of your parent class you have:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>...
&lt;router-outlet [routerOutletData]=&quot;onEvent&quot; /&gt;
...
</code></pre>
<p>In the child component you would then use:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export class ChildComponent {
    emit = (inject(ROUTER_OUTLET_DATA) as Signal&lt;(data: DataType) =&gt; {}&gt;)();

    ...

    // Some event getting triggerd on the child.
    onEvent() {
        // Getting the data you need
        const data: DataType = ...
        // Using Parent function:
        this.emit(data);
    }
}
</code></pre>
